  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Arranged in **ascending order**, the solutions of the equation $2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+2\\sqrt{2}=\\sqrt{2}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}<x\\le {360}^{\u2218},$ are $x=${{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+2\\sqrt{2} & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={135}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${135}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the specified domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={135}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952163/assets/144ed33e7739fbaf17e3f81dd9ae2fd0a2d8e4d622ced7cb5dd60c8d177b6c01.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{45}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={225}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions of the equation, arranged in ascending order, are $x={135}^{\u2218}$ and $x={225}^{\u2218}.$",
